From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retroforge <retroforge@invalid>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 07:40:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(LaunchManager): recent apps are names only

launcher.json's "recent" list held a null (HW, KONKR Pocket FIT,
2026-10-22: {"recent":["Hades",null,"Steam"]}). Play on a home card left
on a replaced library item (patch 0023 fixes that card) saves its launch
item's name, and that card had none: in a release build the script error
carries on with null, and update_recent_apps() put it first. Every reader
then gets a null where a name belongs; the home screen reads each into a
String, which is a script error of its own.

get_recent_apps() now returns names only, and update_recent_apps() drops
anything else when it saves the list, so launcher.json heals at the next
launch.

---
 core/global/launch_manager.gd | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed

--- a/core/global/launch_manager.gd
+++ b/core/global/launch_manager.gd
@@ -440,6 +440,10 @@
 	for app in _persist_data["recent"]:
 		if i > max_recent:
 			break
+		# Names only: the home screen reads each one into a String, and one null in launcher.json
+		# stopped it there, so no recent app showed at all.
+		if not app is String:
+			continue
 		recent.push_back(app)
 		i += 1
 	return recent
@@ -449,7 +453,7 @@
 func update_recent_apps(app: LibraryLaunchItem) -> void:
 	if not "recent" in _persist_data:
 		_persist_data["recent"] = []
-	var recent: Array = _persist_data["recent"]
+	var recent: Array = (_persist_data["recent"] as Array).filter(func(n): return n is String)
 	recent.erase(app.name)
 	recent.push_front(app.name)
 
